<https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/publication/2005_Gaiani_Reverse> a :ScholarlyArticle ;
    kg:anvurClassA "yes" ;
    kg:anvurScientificArea08 "yes" ;
    kg:caseStudyScale <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/scale/sculptural-design> ;
    kg:openAccess "yes" ;
    kg:publicationType "Journal article" ;
    :about <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/keyword/3d-laser-scanning>,
        <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/keyword/digital-survey>,
        <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/keyword/nautical-design>,
        <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/keyword/reverse-modelling> ;
    :abstract "Small and medium sized pleasure boat companies still use traditional artisanal systems to build boats. Once the first model of a fibreglass boat has been produced, later models are usually extensively revised to correct faults not envisaged during the design stage. After the changes, and once the boat is launched, the design has to be reviewed before building further models. This is when it is important to be able to quickly and cheaply reconstruct a digital 3D model of the first hull design and alterations in order to build moulds that can produce shells that have all the last minute changes dictated by experience. The article defines a procedure characterised by simplicity, accuracy and reduced costs compared to traditional methods, applied to the survey of a 6400x2200x820 mm inflatable boat hull mould using an integrated combination of triangulation laser scanner and calibrated digital photogrammetry." ;
    :author ( <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/person/gaiani-marco> <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/person/guidi-gabriele> <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/person/micoli-laura-loredana> <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/person/musio-sale-massimo> <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/person/russo-michele> ) ;
    :datePublished "2005" ;
    :identifier "2005_Gaiani_Reverse" ;
    :inLanguage "ITA/ENG" ;
    :isPartOf <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/venue/disegnare-idee-immagini> ;
    :issn "1123-9247" ;
    :name "Reverse modeling per la nautica: rilievo dello scafo di un gommone con sistemi di scansione 3D a basso costo" ;
    :pagination "82-93" ;
    :sameAs "https://iris.uniroma1.it/handle/11573/905448" ;
    :url "https://dsdra.web.uniroma1.it/sites/default/files/Disegnare%2031_2005.pdf" ;
    :volumeNumber "31" .

