<https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/publication/2024_Cappuccino_AlbergoCatenaEGA> a :ScholarlyArticle ;
    kg:caseStudyScale <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/scale/architectural> ;
    kg:conference [ :location "A Coruña, Galicia, Spain | Porto, Norte, Portugal" ;
            :name "XX Congreso Internacional EGA – Horizontes Gráficos" ;
            :year "2024" ] ;
    kg:openAccess "yes" ;
    kg:publicationType "Conference paper" ;
    :about <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/keyword/cultural-heritage>,
        <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/keyword/digital-survey>,
        <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/keyword/hbim>,
        <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/keyword/reconstructive-bim-modelling> ;
    :abstract "Generally, the integrated application of 3D surveying and BIM modelling methodologies on complex case studies leads to a critical evaluation of the pros and cons of the applied process. Virtual 3D models can become a knowledge repository and flexible communication tools to highlight the historical evolution of the building as well as its material and technological articulation. The article proposes a complete knowledge path framed in the representation domain and applied to a stratified medieval artefact—the Albergo della Catena in Rome—up to its new virtual reconfiguration, analysing the geometric and material complexities. The virtual representation towards knowledge and heritage promotion represents the final aim of the project." ;
    :author ( <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/person/cappuccino-francesco> <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/person/flenghi-giulia> <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/person/russo-michele> ) ;
    :contentLocation <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/place/rome-lazio-italy> ;
    :datePublished "2024" ;
    :identifier "2024_Cappuccino_AlbergoCatenaEGA" ;
    :inLanguage "ENG" ;
    :isPartOf <https://micheler77.github.io/publications-kg/venue/horizontes-graficos-xx-congreso-internacional-ega> ;
    :name "Integrated 3D survey and modeling techniques for medieval architectures: The Albergo of the Catena in Rome" ;
    :pagination "421-425" ;
    :publisher "Universidade da Coruña" ;
    :sameAs "https://doi.org/10.17979/spudc.000027" ;
    :url "https://ruc.udc.es/handle/2183/36090" .

